Hello,

I am Joshua Hyrman, and go by Josh. I am an amateur linguist, and have
"dabbled" in German and Spanish, and am currently studying Japanese and
(now) Lojban. I previously attempted Esperanto, but have not pursued it.

I have several years of experience in computer programming, primarily with
PHP and Java. The logical structure of Lojban is what attracts me to it more
than Esperanto.

I live in Vancouver, WA (across from Portland, OR), and would be open to
meeting any other Lojbanists in the Vanouver/Portland area.

I am going through the Introductory Guide, and soon hope to be conversing on
the Lojban-only list.

Josh

